[
    {
        "content": "<p>Inspired by the discussion in <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"287929\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/letI.2FhaveI.20linter/with/610697669\">#mathlib4 &gt; letI/haveI linter</a>, I wondered if there are linters that search through the info trees that don't need to do so, or that could do so more efficiently.</p>\n<p>In particular, I found that the <code>show</code> linter traverses info trees. In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41761\">#41761</a>, I refactor it to avoid this, which gives a <code>0.75%</code> speedup of mathlib.</p>\n<p>I also noticed that the flexible linter, tactic analysis, multi goal linter and unused tactic linter each traverse the info trees individually. I'd think that we should be able to merge some of these.</p>",
        "id": 610705175,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1784082639
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This pattern of embedding the lint into the tactic is interesting, are there many other places this pattern is/could be applied? Maybe a brief bit of documentation explaining the performance motivation would be helpful to leave.</p>\n<p>I also wonder how this fits with tactic analysis linters, which can also guard based on syntax. I'm guessing that still has some extra performance overhead?</p>",
        "id": 610745753,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1784103247
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41804\">#41804</a> I speed up the info tree traversal of the unused tactic linter, which gives a <code>0.41%</code> speedup in mathlib.</p>",
        "id": 610975321,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1784172708
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">my</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">awesome</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proof</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 612805647,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1785055176
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To minimize a bit:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Command</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabShow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">newType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Term</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TacticM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">newType</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">«</span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"bp\">»</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"show \"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newType</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">elabShow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">newType</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">show</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arbitrary_ident</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is the relevant portion of <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41761\">#41761</a> that allows the unresolved name (so the proof becomes <code>sorry</code>), where the core <code>show</code> would instead fail immediately.</p>",
        "id": 612809535,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1785060118
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In today's Meta Cafe we narrowed down the cause of this. <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"548935\">@Thomas Murrills</span> and others could explain the details better, but it boils down to the behavior of:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"bar\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean.Elab.Term.elabTerm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">none</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Lean.logError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"this log sometimes dropped...\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">!</span><span class=\"s2\">\"{e}\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kd\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arbitrary</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When <code>e</code> contains a synthetic <code>sorry</code> in combination with there being two matching parses, it causes the message from <code>Lean.logError</code> and <code>unknownIdentifier</code> to be suppressed. You can see this a few ways:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>commenting out <code>arbitrary</code></li>\n<li>commenting out the <code>throwError</code></li>\n<li>editing the <code>throwError</code> to not have a synthetic <code>sorry</code></li>\n<li>removing the first <code>elab</code></li>\n<li>increasing the priority of one of the <code>elab</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>The conclusion that we reached at the end of the meeting was that in the short to medium term, it would make sense to be explicit and raise the priority in this case. I've opened <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42264\">#42264</a> making this change and adding Snir's example as a test case.</p>",
        "id": 613525232,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1785361582
    }
]